# Stub for libhwy, required only to satisfy pkg-config.
#
# The SDK at /opt/fus-imx-disco/5.15-kirkstone ships libjxl 0.10.2 whose
# libjxl.pc declares `Requires.private: libhwy`, but the sysroot contains no
# libhwy at all -- no .pc, no library, no headers -- so `meson setup` fails
# before it can configure anything.
#
# Requires.private matters only for STATIC linking, and hwy is not needed here:
#   - libjxl.so.0.10.2 has no DT_NEEDED entry for libhwy (hwy is linked in
#     statically), verified with objdump -p;
#   - no header under sysroot usr/include/jxl includes hwy/;
#   - the board carries libjxl 0.10.2 and 0.12.0 and no libhwy whatsoever.
#
# So an empty stub is accurate rather than a workaround that hides a real gap.
# Use with:  PKG_CONFIG_PATH=tools/pkgconfig-overlay:$PKG_CONFIG_PATH
#
# The clean fix is to install a real libhwy into the SDK sysroot; until then
# this keeps the module build reproducible.

Name: libhwy
Description: Stub - hwy is statically linked into libjxl in this SDK
Version: 1.0.0
Cflags:
Libs:
